      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note: LynnReal Flash 3-step DMD",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## LynnReal Flash · 3-step DMD (ref2v)\n\nReference-driven generation with audio: one or more reference pictures, then the Flash checkpoint at its trained three steps.\n\n- `UNETLoader`: `lynnreal_omni_flash_int8.safetensors` — 42 blocks, trained W8A8\n- `LynnRealFlashTokenCompression`: blocks 2–27 run on the stride-2 spatial subset of the video rows, block 28 restores the full sequence (a dropped row takes its nearest same-timestep anchor's update)\n- `MiniMaxH3ReferenceToVideo`: the reference pictures ride their own spatial grids; the stride is applied per grid, so the generated rows keep their quarter\n- `ref_image_size`: `max` (2048 short edge), the release's reference preparation\n- `BasicScheduler`: `simple`, **3 steps**, `euler`\n\n**Speed** (H100, hot, 1344x768, 3 steps, mean of 3 runs; the release's *generate wall* — first\ndenoiser forward to decoded frames, without loading, compilation or encoding)\n\n| task | 5s | 10s |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| t2v | 8.41s | 22.01s |\n| ti2v | 8.90s | 23.05s |\n| ref2v | 9.54s | 24.22s |\n\nEnd to end (click Run → finished, warm) adds about 3.7s at 5s and 7.1s at 10s: prompt and\nconditioning encoding, then muxing.\n\n**Precision — W8A8 INT8**\n\nThe 252 quantized projections keep their exported INT8 rows and per-output-channel scales:\nComfyUI loads them as `int8_tensorwise` and runs `int8_linear`, which quantizes activations per\ntoken, accumulates in INT32 and dequantizes in FP32 — the same contract as the release's\n`model/int8.py`. The remaining 60 modules stay BF16, as exported. On this torch (cu126) the\nnode pack enables comfy-kitchen's Triton backend and pins its GEMM config, so a prompt edit no\nlonger re-tunes the kernels before the first step.\n\n**Links**\n\n- Code: https://github.com/LynnReal-AI/LynnReal-Omni\n- Paper: https://huggingface.co/papers/2609.15863\n- Weights: https://huggingface.co/stdstu123/LynnReal-Onmi-beta-0.1\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
